# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the platform. A Windows checkout
# was giving them CRLF, and Linux then refuses to run them at all — the shebang
# resolves to `bash\r`, which is not a program. That made benchmarks/run_all.sh
# unrunnable in a container built from a Windows working copy, which is how the
# 30-task suite came to sit un-rerun for months.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else executed by a POSIX interpreter.
*.bash text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
